 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And, as a king mine array,\nI took my armed forces and set away.\nFor the sun came down in the morning he\nHad sent me forth alone, we\nSleeped on in our array\nTo quench this day's young white flame with decay.\nBut now the middle star of all creation,\nThat began its birth at dawn undone,\nHas trampled us. Light is away\nFrom here to heaven; decay\nIs fallen from men's doors towards creation.\nThere, where night's horn has reached out again",
